# BarMitzva Project Rules (.cursorrules)
# "El Bar de Medina" — Interactive Bar Mitzva party app

## Project
- Expo / React Native app (SDK 54, React 19, TypeScript)
- Firebase: Firestore (DB name: "barmitzvamedina"), Storage, Anonymous Auth
- Backend: Node.js + Socket.IO for multiplayer Pacman
- Routing: expo-router (file-based)

## Directory Map
- `app/` — Screens (expo-router file-based routing)
- `app/(tabs)/` — Tab navigator (Home, Games)
- `app/games/` — Game screens (pacman, roulette, soccer, trivia)
- `app/social/` — Social features (messages, homenajes)
- `app/admin/` — Admin panel (PIN protected)
- `app/dashboard/` — Projector dashboard
- `backend/` — Pacman multiplayer Node.js server
- `services/` — Firebase + Socket.IO services
- `components/` — Shared React Native components
- `constants/theme.ts` — Colors and fonts
- `functions/` — Firebase Cloud Functions

## Conventions
- Use `StyleSheet.create()` for styles
- Colors: `Colors.elegant.*` (dark theme), `Colors.river.*` (red), `Colors.macabi.*` (blue)
- Fonts: `Fonts.sans`, `Fonts.bold`, `Fonts.light` (Montserrat)
- Dark theme default: bg `#121212`, text white, accent gold `#D4AF37`
- All Firestore ops via `services/database.ts`
- Socket ops via `services/pacmanSocket.ts` singleton
- Score: call `updatePlayerScore(points)` — cumulative
- Auth: Anonymous Firebase sign-in on app load
- Data: `onSnapshot` for real-time, return unsubscribe
- Navigation: `useRouter()` → `push()` / `replace()` / `back()`
- Always `sanitize()` data before Firestore writes

## Games
1. **Pacman Gigante** — Multiplayer (Socket.IO), lobby + game screen, joystick/keyboard
2. **Trivia Medina** — 5 questions, timer, score
3. **La Ruleta** — Spinning animation, random dare, camera
4. **Hacele un Caño** — Soccer, movement + shooting + collision

## Firebase Collections
scores, profiles, messages, news, homenajes, media, configs, tokens

## Run
- Frontend: `npx expo start --web` (port 8081)
- Backend: `cd backend && npm run dev` (port 3000)
- Deploy web: `npx expo export --platform web && vercel --prod`
- Deploy Firebase: `firebase deploy`
